    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0721" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.61317/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-23T20:00:00-03:00">July 23, 1943—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3570. My 3355, July 10, 2 p.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d661-f1"/> Minister of
                        Finance<anchor n="8" xml:id="d661-f2"/> yesterday stated that before July 31
                    he would like assurance regarding rice <pb facs="0722" n="710" xml:id="pg710"/>
                    purchase agreement as basis Government financing Rio Grande do Sul crop to be
                    planted in August. Foreign Office also has again inquired about agreement.</p>
                <p>British Embassy advises that Richard Bland, rice expert of Ministry of Food,
                    shortly is coming to Brazil in company with representatives Commodity Credit
                    Corporation who are interested in buying other commodities under agreements to
                    be negotiated with Brazilian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
